---Typed view over the Subscription.delivery_config JSON blob.
---@class posthog.subscriptions.DeliveryConfig
---@field post_all_insights_in_main_message? boolean Slack subscriptions only. Insight and dashboard subscriptions: when true, upload all insight images together in the main Slack message instead of posting the first image in the main message and the rest as threaded replies. Prompt subscriptions: when true, post the chart images in the main message with the summary; when false, post them in the first thread reply. Defaults to false. The request is rejected when target_type is not 'slack', or when an insight or dashboard subscription's Slack integration does not hold the files:write permission. Omit it unless the user asks for all images or charts in the main message.
---@field include_images? boolean Prompt subscriptions only: include generated chart images. Defaults to true when omitted. The request is rejected when the subscription sets insight or dashboard instead of prompt. It does not control the AI summary on an insight or dashboard subscription: use summary_enabled and summary_prompt_guide for that.
---@field include_feedback? boolean Prompt subscriptions only: include report feedback links. Defaults to true when omitted. The request is rejected when the subscription sets insight or dashboard instead of prompt. It does not control the AI summary on an insight or dashboard subscription: use summary_enabled and summary_prompt_guide for that.
---@field include_manage_link? boolean Prompt subscriptions only: include a link to manage the subscription. Defaults to true when omitted. The request is rejected when the subscription sets insight or dashboard instead of prompt. It does not control the AI summary on an insight or dashboard subscription: use summary_enabled and summary_prompt_guide for that.
---@field include_posthog_hint? boolean Prompt subscriptions only: include PostHog product guidance. Defaults to true when omitted. Only a Slack report renders the guidance. Email and Microsoft Teams reports leave it out and accept the option without an error, unlike post_all_insights_in_main_message. The request is rejected when the subscription sets insight or dashboard instead of prompt. It does not control the AI summary on an insight or dashboard subscription: use summary_enabled and summary_prompt_guide for that.

