---@field prompt? string|distilled.Null Free-text prompt that drives the AI-generated report. Required when resource_type is 'ai_prompt'. Max 4000 characters.
---@field ai_prompt_config? posthog.subscriptions.AIPromptConfig Configuration for AI report subscriptions (analysis window, future knobs). Only valid when resource_type is 'ai_prompt'. Replaced wholesale on writes.
---@field contexts? posthog.subscriptions.UpdateSubscriptionRequestContextsList Complete dashboard and insight context for an AI report. Omit on PATCH to preserve, pass an empty list to clear, or pass up to 3 items to replace all contexts.
---@field target_type posthog.subscriptions.SubscriptionTargetEnum|string Delivery channel: email, slack, or teams. * `email` - Email * `slack` - Slack * `teams` - Microsoft Teams
---@field target_value string Recipient(s): comma-separated email addresses for email, Slack channel name/ID for slack, or a Microsoft Teams webhook URL for teams. A Teams webhook URL is only ever returned as its host, because the URL authorizes a post to the channel by itself. On update, omit the field to keep the stored URL, or send a full URL to replace it.
---@field frequency posthog.subscriptions.RecurrenceIntervalEnum|string How often to deliver: daily, weekly, monthly, or yearly. * `daily` - Daily * `weekly` - Weekly * `monthly` - Monthly * `yearly` - Yearly
---@field interval number Interval multiplier (e.g. 2 with weekly frequency means every 2 weeks). Required on create; must be 1 or greater.
---@field byweekday? posthog.subscriptions.UpdateSubscriptionRequestByweekdayList|distilled.Null Days of week for daily or weekly subscriptions: monday, tuesday, wednesday, thursday, friday, saturday, sunday.
---@field bysetpos? number|distilled.Null Position within byweekday set for monthly frequency (e.g. 1 for first, -1 for last).
---@field count? number|distilled.Null Total number of deliveries before the subscription stops. Null for unlimited.
---@field start_date string When to start delivering (ISO 8601 datetime). The date anchors the recurrence and may be in the past. Deliveries run on half-hour cycles at :00 and :30. Other minute values are accepted for backward compatibility, but delivery happens during the next cycle instead of at that exact minute.
---@field until_date? string|distilled.Null When to stop delivering (ISO 8601 datetime). Null for indefinite.
---@field deleted? boolean Set to true to soft-delete. Subscriptions cannot be hard-deleted.
---@field enabled? boolean Whether the subscription is active. Set to false to pause delivery without deleting. Auto-set to false when the delivery integration becomes invalid.
---@field title? string|distilled.Null Human-readable name for this subscription.
---@field integration_id? number|distilled.Null ID of a connected Slack integration. Required when target_type is slack.
---@field invite_message? string|distilled.Null Optional message included in the invitation email when adding new recipients.
---@field send_test_now? boolean Whether to immediately deliver the subscription once on save so the editor can confirm it looks right. Defaults to true on create. When omitted on update, a delivery is sent only if the edit changed what gets delivered (recipient, channel, source) or re-enabled the subscription. The recurring schedule is unaffected.
---@field summary_enabled? boolean Whether to attach an AI-generated summary to each delivery (insight and dashboard subscriptions only). Requires the organization to have approved AI data processing, and is subject to the org's active-summary cap and AI credit budget; otherwise the write is rejected. Not applicable to prompt subscriptions, which are themselves AI-generated.
---@field summary_prompt_guide? string Optional free-text guidance (max 500 chars) steering the AI summary, e.g. which metrics to emphasize. Only settable when AI summary context is enabled for the organization; clearing it (empty string) is always allowed.
---@field delivery_config? posthog.subscriptions.DeliveryConfig Per-delivery rendering options. Every option applies to one subscription kind or delivery target only, and each option's own description says where it applies and whether a mismatch is rejected or ignored. Omit this field unless the user asks for one of the options.

